      <main id="content"><article class="proof-reader" data-authored-declaration="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.GibbsGradientMean.integrable_gradient_and_integral_eq_zero"><div class="eyebrow">Samplinglib mathematical lesson</div><h1>Actual Gibbs gradient has zero mean</h1><p><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.GibbsGradientMean.integrable_gradient_and_integral_eq_zero</code> · theorem · <a href="index.html">Teaching coverage</a></p><section class="reader-first-pass" aria-label="First reading"><div class="reader-first-pass-label">Read this first</div><h2>Mathematical statement</h2><p class="reader-claim">The actual normalized Gibbs volume tilt exp(-U) is a probability measure, its genuine vector gradient is Bochner integrable, and its mean is zero under the stated C2 positive-lower/finite-upper Hessian assumptions.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation reader-main-equation">\[\mu=(dx)^{e^{-U}},\quad\mu(E)=1,\quad\nabla U\in L^1(\mu),\quad\int\nabla U\,d\mu=0.\]</div><h3>Proof roadmap</h3><ol class="proof-roadmap"><li><span>1</span><strong>Produce the genuine Gibbs domains</strong><p>Internally widen the upper bound to max(alpha,beta) only when invoking the existing score-square producer. Its actual probability and gradient norm-square L1 give vector MemLp2 and Bochner L1. The shared theorem has no alpha&lt;=beta premise; the dimension-zero case is retained.</p></li><li><span>2</span><strong>Recover ordinary full-space weighted integrability</strong><p>The canonical curvature-to-strong-convexity and Gibbs integrability providers yield integrable exp(-U) against ordinary volume. The actual tilted-law equivalence converts gradient L1 into exp(-U) times gradient L1 against this same volume. Its directional inner product is integrable for every v.</p></li><li><span>3</span><strong>Integrate the derivative against the constant function</strong><p>C2 gives the ordinary Frechet chain rule Dw[v]=-w inner(gradientU,v). Apply full-space directional integration by parts to w and the constant1. All three required integrable products have been derived; the constant derivative is zero. No pointwise boundary-value or cutoff condition is assumed.</p></li><li><span>4</span><strong>Normalize and reconstruct the zero vector mean</strong><p>The canonical tilt integral divides each directional cancellation by the produced finite positive partition. Inner-product/integral commutation and real Hilbert extensionality identify the vector mean as zero. All objects use the same actual Gibbs measure.</p></li></ol></section><details class="reader-ledger assumption-ledger"><summary>Full assumptions and notation</summary><h3>All objects and hypotheses</h3><ul><li>Complete finite-dimensional real Hilbert E with canonical volume and Borel structure; dimension zero included.</li><li>Actual C2 potential U with positive NNReal alpha lower Hessian bound and finite NNReal beta upper bound, no alpha&lt;=beta assumption. No supplied probability, partition, minimizer, regularity/domain/IBP certificate or mean identity.</li></ul><p class="muted"></p></details><h2>Mathematical proof</h2><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>1. Produce the genuine Gibbs domains</h4><p>Internally widen the upper bound to max(alpha,beta) only when invoking the existing score-square producer. Its actual probability and gradient norm-square L1 give vector MemLp2 and Bochner L1. The shared theorem has no alpha&lt;=beta premise; the dimension-zero case is retained.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\bar\beta=\max(\alpha,\beta),\quad\mu\propto e^{-U}dx,\quad\nabla U\in L^2(\mu)\subset L^1(\mu).\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>GibbsGradientMoment.gibbs_gradient_moment; memLp_two_iff_integrable_sq_norm; MemLp.integrable</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>2. Recover ordinary full-space weighted integrability</h4><p>The canonical curvature-to-strong-convexity and Gibbs integrability providers yield integrable exp(-U) against ordinary volume. The actual tilted-law equivalence converts gradient L1 into exp(-U) times gradient L1 against this same volume. Its directional inner product is integrable for every v.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[w=e^{-U},\quad w\in L^1(dx),\quad w\nabla U\in L^1(dx),\quad w\langle\nabla U,v\rangle\in L^1(dx).\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>QuadraticRegularization.strongConvexOn_and_lipschitzWith_gradient_add_quadratic; StrongConvexGibbsIntegrability.integrable_exp_neg_of_strongConvexOn; integrable_tilted_iff; Integrable.inner_const</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>3. Integrate the derivative against the constant function</h4><p>C2 gives the ordinary Frechet chain rule Dw[v]=-w inner(gradientU,v). Apply full-space directional integration by parts to w and the constant1. All three required integrable products have been derived; the constant derivative is zero. No pointwise boundary-value or cutoff condition is assumed.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[Dw(x)[v]=-w(x)\langle\nabla U(x),v\rangle,\quad\int w\langle\nabla U,v\rangle dx=0.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>integral_mul_fderiv_eq_neg_fderiv_mul_of_integrable; fderiv_const_apply</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>4. Normalize and reconstruct the zero vector mean</h4><p>The canonical tilt integral divides each directional cancellation by the produced finite positive partition. Inner-product/integral commutation and real Hilbert extensionality identify the vector mean as zero. All objects use the same actual Gibbs measure.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\int\langle v,\nabla U\rangle d\mu=0\quad(\forall v),\qquad\int\nabla U\,d\mu=0.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>integral_tilted; integral_div; integral_eq_zero_of_forall_integral_inner_eq_zero</p></details></div><section class="lean-verification"><h2>Lean verification</h2><p>The exact proposition and proof begin folded so the mathematical argument remains the primary reading path.</p><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-statement" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.GibbsGradientMean.integrable_gradient_and_integral_eq_zero"><summary>Lean statement · integrable_gradient_and_integral_eq_zero</summary><p>The actual normalized Gibbs volume tilt exp(-U) is a probability measure, its genuine vector gradient is Bochner integrable, and its mean is zero under the stated C2 positive-lower/finite-upper Hessian assumptions.</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem integrable_gradient_and_integral_eq_zero
    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    {U : E → ℝ} {α β : ℝ≥0} (hα : 0 &lt; α) (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)
    (hH : ∀ x v : E, (α : ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x v v ≤ (β : ℝ)*‖v‖^2) :
    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -U x)
    IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧ Integrable (gradient U) μ ∧
      (∫ x, gradient U x ∂μ) = 0</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-gibbsgradientmean.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-proof" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.GibbsGradientMean.integrable_gradient_and_integral_eq_zero"><summary>Lean proof · integrable_gradient_and_integral_eq_zero</summary><p>Produce the genuine Gibbs domains; Recover ordinary full-space weighted integrability; Integrate the derivative against the constant function; Normalize and reconstruct the zero vector mean</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem integrable_gradient_and_integral_eq_zero
    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    {U : E → ℝ} {α β : ℝ≥0} (hα : 0 &lt; α) (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)
    (hH : ∀ x v : E, (α : ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x v v ≤ (β : ℝ)*‖v‖^2) :
    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -U x)
    IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧ Integrable (gradient U) μ ∧
      (∫ x, gradient U x ∂μ) = 0 := by
  let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -U x)
  have hupper : ∀ x v : E,
      (α : ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x v v ≤ ((max α β : ℝ≥0) : ℝ)*‖v‖^2 := by
    intro x v
    refine ⟨(hH x v).1,(hH x v).2.trans ?_⟩
    exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (by exact_mod_cast le_max_right α β) (sq_nonneg _)
  have hm := GibbsGradientMoment.gibbs_gradient_moment hα (le_max_left α β) hU hupper
  have hμ : IsProbabilityMeasure μ := hm.1
  let : IsProbabilityMeasure μ := hμ
  have hc : Continuous (gradient U) :=
    Calculus.Gradient.continuous_gradient_of_contDiff_one (hU.of_le (by norm_num))
  have hlp : MemLp (gradient U) 2 μ :=
    (memLp_two_iff_integrable_sq_norm hc.aestronglyMeasurable).mpr hm.2.1
  have hg : Integrable (gradient U) μ := hlp.integrable (by norm_num)
  have hd : Differentiable ℝ U := hU.differentiable (by norm_num)
  have hs := QuadraticRegularization.strongConvexOn_and_lipschitzWith_gradient_add_quadratic
    (r := 0) hU hH (0 : E)
  simp only [NNReal.coe_zero,zero_div,zero_mul,add_zero] at hs
  have hi := StrongConvexGibbsIntegrability.integrable_exp_neg_of_strongConvexOn
    (show (0 : ℝ) &lt; α from hα) hd hs.1
  have hweighted : Integrable (fun x =&gt; Real.exp (-U x) • gradient U x)
      (volume : Measure E) := (integrable_tilted_iff hi _).mp hg
  refine ⟨hμ,hg,integral_eq_zero_of_forall_integral_inner_eq_zero ℝ _ hg ?_⟩
  intro v
  change (∫ x, inner ℝ v (gradient U x) ∂μ) = 0
  rw [show (fun x =&gt; inner ℝ v (gradient U x)) =
      (fun x =&gt; inner ℝ (gradient U x) v) by funext x; exact real_inner_comm _ _]
  let f := fun x =&gt; Real.exp (-U x)
  have hf : Differentiable ℝ f := hd.neg.exp
  have hfd (x : E) : fderiv ℝ f x v = -f x*inner ℝ (gradient U x) v := by
    rw [show fderiv ℝ f x = _ from (hd x).hasFDerivAt.neg.exp.fderiv]
    simp only [smul_apply,neg_apply,smul_eq_mul,Pi.neg_apply]
    rw [← inner_gradient_left]
    dsimp only [f]
    ring
  have hwv : Integrable (fun x =&gt; f x*inner ℝ (gradient U x) v)
      (volume : Measure E) := by
    simpa only [real_inner_smul_left,f] using hweighted.inner_const (𝕜 := ℝ) v
  have hdf : Integrable (fun x =&gt; fderiv ℝ f x v*(1 : ℝ))
      (volume : Measure E) := by
    convert hwv.neg using 1
    ext x
    rw [hfd]
    change (-f x*inner ℝ (gradient U x) v)*1 = -(f x*inner ℝ (gradient U x) v)
    ring
  have hb := integral_mul_fderiv_eq_neg_fderiv_mul_of_integrable hdf
    (by simp) (by simpa only [mul_one] using hi)
    (fun x _ =&gt; hf x) (fun x _ =&gt; differentiableAt_const (1 : ℝ))
  have hzero : (∫ x, f x*inner ℝ (gradient U x) v ∂(volume : Measure E)) = 0 := by
    simpa [hfd,neg_mul,integral_neg] using hb.symm
  rw [show μ = (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -U x) from rfl,integral_tilted]
  rw [show (fun x =&gt; (Real.exp (-U x)/(∫ z,Real.exp (-U z))) •
      inner ℝ (gradient U x) v) = (fun x =&gt; (f x*inner ℝ (gradient U x) v)/
        (∫ z,Real.exp (-U z))) by funext x; simp only [smul_eq_mul,f]; ring]
  rw [integral_div,hzero,zero_div]

end AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.GibbsGradientMean</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-gibbsgradientmean.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details></section><details class="reader-ledger boundary-ledger"><summary>Scope and omitted-condition boundaries</summary><ul><li>Only actual Gibbs gradient mean zero and source3.1/S4.Ex9 genuine smoothed-score/posterior/standardized-chain identity. No supplied means/moments/normalizers/IBP/gradient equality/selector; exact eta&gt;0. No bias4.2, FIRST4.6W2/LSI/T2, fullLemma4.2, algorithm/work/main/composition credit. Actual RGO law is not Gaussian gradient-output or HMC. Focused3751 passed, standard3 only; independent math/blind/source/exactcommit/publication/integration admission pending. RenderedQA, Copy/Download implementation and postmerge purification remain open.</li></ul></details><details class="proof-reader-provenance reader-ledger"><summary>Sources, dependencies, and reuse</summary><h2>Source and reuse</h2><h3>Samplinglib parents called</h3><ul><li><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-gibbsgradientmoment.html#decl-autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-gibbsgradientmoment-gibbs-gr-45d2759e97"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.GibbsGradientMoment.gibbs_gradient_moment</code></a></li><li><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-strongconvexgibbsintegrability.html#decl-autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-strongconvexgibbsintegrabili-51ed1587ae"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.StrongConvexGibbsIntegrability.integrable_exp_neg_of_strongConvexOn</code></a></li><li><a href="../theorems/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-calculus-gradient-continuous-gradient-of-contdiff-one.html"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.Calculus.Gradient.continuous_gradient_of_contDiff_one</code></a></li><li><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-quadraticregularization.html#decl-autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-quadraticregularization-stro-17eea540ae"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.QuadraticRegularization.strongConvexOn_and_lipschitzWith_gradient_add_quadratic</code></a></li></ul><h3>Mathlib API called (external library)</h3><ul><li>integral_mul_fderiv_eq_neg_fderiv_mul_of_integrable</li><li>MeasureTheory.integrable_tilted_iff</li><li>MeasureTheory.integral_tilted</li><li>integral_eq_zero_of_forall_integral_inner_eq_zero</li></ul><h3>Mathematical sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.Ex9">Exact source mean identity and its internal analytic background</a> — Only actual Gibbs gradient mean zero and source3.1/S4.Ex9 genuine smoothed-score/posterior/standardized-chain identity. No supplied means/moments/normalizers/IBP/gradient equality/selector; exact eta&gt;0. No bias4.2, FIRST4.6W2/LSI/T2, fullLemma4.2, algorithm/work/main/composition credit. Actual RGO law is not Gaussian gradient-output or HMC. Focused3751 passed, standard3 only; independent math/blind/source/exactcommit/publication/integration admission pending. RenderedQA, Copy/Download implementation and postmerge purification remain open.</li></ul><p>Samplinglib prose is not a quotation or a source-equivalence certificate. Definitions and aliases are explained as constructions, not counted as new mathematical proofs.</p></details></article></main>
